<title>ITALY: Italy's Trieste sees Sept CPI at 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Trieste sees Sept CPI at 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TRIESTE, Italy 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Trieste said its September consumer price index stood at 0.7 percent month-on-month and 3.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In August, Trieste's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 2.6 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Trieste is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.49 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to August 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.7   (0.1)     3.0  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.1   (0.3)     4.3  (5.0)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.4   (0.0)     3.9  (4.7)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.3   (0.4)     4.8  (4.7)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.5   (0.5)     2.9  (3.2)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2   (0.0)     1.5  (1.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.1   (0.2)     3.1  (3.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     5.4   (0.1)     3.0 (-2.0)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.5   (0.5)     2.4  (3.2)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.1   (0.1)     4.0  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0   (0.0)     0.0  (0.0)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom ++392 66129526</p>
